Neither table matches this unit's fan. In practice it has two speeds (~920 and ~1650-1700 rpm), and '''value 2 stops it''', although both tables list value 2 as a running speed. The default left by U-Boot (and what gpio-fan reports, &quot;3800&quot;) is value 3, about 920 rpm.

The DT therefore lists '''all eight values in DSM's order''', labelled with the measured speeds, so <code>ds212j-fan</code> (step 13) can select exactly the level DSM would, by index through <code>pwm1</code>:

<pre class="dts">gpio-fan,speed-map = &lt;   0 0&gt;, &lt; 925 1&gt;, &lt;   0 2&gt;, &lt; 920 3&gt;,
                     &lt;1620 4&gt;, &lt;1690 5&gt;, &lt;1640 6&gt;, &lt;1700 7&gt;;</pre>
The value U-Boot leaves on the pins (3) must be in the table, or <code>gpio-fan</code> refuses to probe (<code>missing speed array entry for GPIO value 0x…</code>).

<span id="checking-the-dtb-on-the-nas"></span>
=== Checking the DTB on the NAS ===

<code>tools/build-kernel-deb.sh</code> applies the patch, <code>make bindeb-pkg</code> ships the DTB in <code>/usr/lib/linux-image-&lt;version&gt;/kirkwood-ds212j.dtb</code>, and <code>u-boot-menu</code> points <code>extlinux.conf</code> at it (<code>fdt …</code>). U-Boot loads it, fixes up the memory size and MAC address, and passes it to the kernel. To see what the running system actually uses:

<pre>dtc -I dtb -O dts /usr/lib/linux-image-$(uname -r)/kirkwood-ds212j.dtb | less
ls /proc/device-tree/                       # the live tree the kernel booted with
cat /sys/kernel/debug/pinctrl/*/pinmux-pins # who owns each MPP (mount debugfs first)</pre>
